# MUST BE INCONSISTENT: the data of the AI subdomain and the payload of the
# communication subdomain are disjoint.
#
# This is the equivalence the information model of the dissertation assumed
# and which ALIGNMENT.md argues against. ISO/IEC 7498-1, 5.6.1.2 defines user
# data as the payload of one transmission, ISO/IEC 22989 defines data as a
# collection of samples. A dataset travels many times and keeps its identity,
# a payload does not.
#
# The alignment relates the two with carriesData instead, and this model is
# what the axiom behind that decision rejects.
@prefix aias:     <https://w3id.org/aias#> .
@prefix vdi3682:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#> .
@prefix iso7498:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#> .
@prefix iso22989: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#> .
@prefix ex:       <https://w3id.org/aias/example/neg#> .
@prefix owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/example/neg04> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/aias/2.0.0> .
ex:Thing4 a iso22989:Data , iso7498:UserData .
